  fix:   see 'warden build --driver firecracker --help' for the flags this driver takes
warden build --driver vz --guest-os windows
  error: --guest-os windows is currently only supported by --driver qemu or --driver hyperv
warden build --driver firecracker --guest-os windows
  error: --guest-os windows is currently only supported by --driver qemu or --driver hyperv
warden build --guest-os plan9
  error: invalid --guest-os "plan9" (want "linux" or "windows")
warden build --driver nomad
  error: driver "nomad" not found (searched PATH, then $WARDEN_DIR, where warden is installed)
  fix:   put warden-driver-nomad on PATH or beside warden, or name its file: --driver /path/to/warden-driver-nomad. `warden driver list` shows the drivers warden can find
warden build --timeout soon
  error: invalid --timeout: time: invalid duration "soon"
  fix:   give a Go duration such as 30s, 10m or 1h
warden build --capture everything
  error: invalid capture mode "everything" (valid: none, headers, bodies, all)
warden build --driver qemu --build-link 10.9.0.0/24
  error: --build-link: 10.9.0.0/24 is a /24; the build link must be a /30
  fix:   pass --build-link a valid /30, e.g. --build-link 100.126.255.252/30
warden build --regoin eu
  error: unknown flag --regoin for driver "container"
  fix:   see 'warden build --driver container --help' for the flags this driver takes
warden build a b
  error: accepts at most 1 arg(s), received 2
  fix:   see 'warden build --help'
warden build
  error: no Dockerfile or Containerfile found in $CTX
  fix:   pass the Dockerfile's path, or the directory that holds it
warden build --driver qemu
  error: nothing to build in $CTX: pass --script, or add build.sh or a Dockerfile
warden build --driver hyperv --guest-os windows
  error: nothing to build in $CTX: pass --script, or add build.ps1
warden build  (warden.toml: "[runtime]\ndriver = \"nomad\"\n")
  error: driver "nomad" not found (searched PATH, then $WARDEN_DIR, where warden is installed)
  fix:   put warden-driver-nomad on PATH or beside warden, or name its file: --driver /path/to/warden-driver-nomad. `warden driver list` shows the drivers warden can find
warden build  (warden.toml: "[runtime]\nrelay_image = \"-x\"\n")
  error: [runtime] relay_image in $CTX/warden.toml is "-x": not an image reference
  fix:   set it to an image reference such as ghcr.io/buildwarden/relay:v0.2.0 or to "dev", or remove it
warden build --driver qemu  (warden.toml: "[vm]\nimage_refresh_after = \"soon\"\n")
  error: $CTX/warden.toml [vm] image_refresh_after: invalid age "soon"
  fix:   set it to an age such as "7d" or "36h"
warden build --driver qemu  (warden.toml: "[vm]\nimage_min_grace = \"soon\"\n")
  error: $CTX/warden.toml [vm] image_min_grace: invalid age "soon"
  fix:   set it to an age such as "7d" or "36h"
warden build --driver qemu  (warden.toml: "[vm]\nbuild_link = \"10.9.0.0/24\"\n")
  error: [vm] build_link in $CTX/warden.toml: 10.9.0.0/24 is a /24; the build link must be a /30
  fix:   set [vm] build_link in $CTX/warden.toml to a valid /30, e.g. build_link = "100.126.255.252/30", or remove it to use the default
warden build  (warden.toml: "[Runtime]\nCLI = \"podman\"\n")
  error: $CTX/warden.toml: [Runtime] CLI: keys are case-sensitive, and the container driver reads [driver.container] cli (old name [runtime] cli)
  fix:   write it as [driver.container] cli
warden build --driver qemu  (warden.toml: "[driver.Qemu]\nimage_refresh_after = \"3d\"\n")
  error: $CTX/warden.toml: [driver.Qemu] image_refresh_after: keys are case-sensitive, and the qemu driver reads [driver.qemu] image_refresh_after
  fix:   write it as [driver.qemu] image_refresh_after
warden build --driver hyperv  (warden.toml: "[vm]\nnetwork = \"a\"\nNetwork = \"b\"\n")
  error: $CTX/warden.toml: [vm] holds network and Network: keys are case-sensitive, and the hyperv driver reads [driver.hyperv] network (old name [vm] network)
  fix:   keep one, written as [driver.hyperv] network
warden build  (warden.toml: "[build]\ncapture = \"everything\"\n")
  error: invalid capture mode "everything" (valid: none, headers, bodies, all)
warden build  (warden.toml: "not toml [")
  error: parsing $CTX/warden.toml: toml: line 1: expected '.' or '=', but got 't' instead
  fix:   fix the TOML syntax in $CTX/warden.toml
